    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1020">

                <pb facs="1182" n="1070" xml:id="pg1070"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5294/579: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-02T12:00:00+09:00">March 2,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 2—2:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. Department’s 28, February 28, 6 p.m. Instructions in paragraph 2 were carried
                    out this morning. The Minister said that he fully understood the considerations
                    set forth and had had them in mind in answering questions both in the Diet and
                    from the press. He assured me that he would continue to avoid giving
                    specifications.</p>
                <p>I did not touch on the point of constitutionality.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
